%N A400353 The lexicographically earliest infinite sequence of distinct integers such that the concatenation of a(n-1)'s last digit, a(n), and a(n+1)'s first digit is a square.
%C A400353 Might be called "sticky squares" since each number "sticks" to the digits adjacent to it in the sequence and forms a square.
%C A400353 a(1) must also create a square with the one adjacent digit it sticks to in a(2).
%C A400353 Is every term of A398629 in this sequence?
%C A400353 The sequence is infinite: At any point, the first digit of a(n) is forced by the previous two terms, so the first two digits of the square centered at n are forced. Since there are infinitely many squares beginning with any 2-digit prefix and not ending in 0 (proof on next line), one should assign a(n) to be the least such square with its first and last digits truncated which has yet to be used.
%C A400353 Let p be a 2-digit prefix. Numbers beginning with p and followed by k other digits are in the range [p*10^k, (p+1)*10^k). Their square roots lie in an interval of length (sqrt(p+1)-sqrt(p))*10^(k/2), which tends to infinity. Hence, for all sufficiently large k, this interval contains an integer which isn't a multiple of 10, so its square begins with p and doesn't end in 0.
%H A400353 Eric Fox, <a href="/A400353/b400353.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A400353 Eric Fox, <a href="/A400353/a400353.txt">Python program</a>
%e A400353 If you have a(1)=1 and a(2)=6, a(3) must begin with 9 to complete 1|6|? as a square.
%e A400353 If a(3) is 9, 6|9|? has no valid completion as a square.
%e A400353 If a(3) is 90, 6|90|? has no valid completion as a square.
%e A400353 If a(3) is 91, 6|91|? has no valid completion as a square.
%e A400353 ...
%e A400353 If a(3) is 916, 6|916|? has a valid completion as a square: 69169, so a(3)=916.
%e A400353 a(3)..a(5) = [916, 969, 60] corresponding to the square number 69696 = 264^2.
%e A400353 a(4)..a(6) = [969, 60, 4] corresponding to the square number 9604 = 98^2.
%e A400353 a(5)..a(7) = [60, 4, 928] corresponding to the square number 049 = 7^2.
